{
  "about": "CC0 models used by Firebird v2, where they come from, and how _pipeline/process.py turns each into a contract-ready .glb (docs/ASSETS.md). Rebuild: node assets/cc0/_pipeline/fetch.mjs, then blender -b -P assets/cc0/_pipeline/process.py, then node assets/cc0/_pipeline/manifest.mjs. Weapons: set \"view\": \"first-person\" only for a model built to be held in view AND fitting the theme; the renderer (fitsView in src/render/renderer.js) uses an authored gun only with that flag and otherwise keeps its built-in one. The Old Earth reskin (STYLE_GUIDE.md) forbids real-world guns, so no CC0 gun is flagged.",
